notes=r'''The sheet compares complementary regular open sets (item 1), then works with two relative opens of a closed K, their common frontier C, and B=U_K intersect boundary K (item 3). The large brace gives interiors, complements and frontier formulas. The heavily revised corollary asks when X_1=complement U_K is locally closed. Archive number 9; no date or title. The written second number is 3, not silently renumbered 2.

The actual phrase “ouverts relatifs de X” is preserved; K is the natural relative ambient space suggested by the equations but is not the written letter. The condition inserted above the brace reads “si B cap C=empty” without a visible closure bar on B. No missing bar or hypothesis is supplied. The trailing mark at item 1(d) is ambiguous between an arrow-like mark and a question mark, and is retained as such rather than interpreted as a definite author objection.

71-010-N1 (targeted counterexample and refinement): item 1(d) alone is not equivalent to (a)-(c). In any nonempty X, U=V=empty satisfies d but fails a and the density assertion in c. Adding X=closure(U union V) to d yields c: d forces U and V disjoint because the common closure intersection is their boundary. Thus the refined statement 71-010-N1r is “d together with density is equivalent to a-c.” This check never changes the written list or its trailing uncertain mark.

71-010-N2 (targeted proof check): for U_K relatively open in closed K, put B=U_K intersect boundary_X K and X_1=X minus U_K. Then Int_X U_K=U_K minus B, so closure_X X_1=X_1 union B. X_1 is locally closed precisely when it is open in its closure, equivalently B is closed in that closed subspace, hence closed in X. With C=closure U_K minus U_K, closure B minus B is contained in C, so the condition is equivalently closure B intersect C=empty. This explains the role of the ambient space but the crop, independently, shows a plain X in the live clause. S row SA01-K71-05 is confirmed at this place; the sweep row itself reported that it had not viewed the image.

The noun before the abbreviated adjective is “sommand,” supported by its single joined word and final tall d, not C’s “sous-ensemble.” Its meaning as a topological summand fits the cancelled decompositions of boundary K into B and B-prime; this linguistic/mathematical comparison helped read the fused middle strokes. “topolog” remains under doubt. The operation in the final U_K/V_K formula is overwritten and is left cup/amalg, even though H regularizes it to cup. The final boundary dot is placed at the upper right of K as written.
'''
checks=[dict(statement_id='71-010-N1 / item 1(d)',type='refuted, with refined id 71-010-N1r',outcome='U=V=empty on nonempty X satisfies d but not a-c; density is missing from d alone.'),dict(statement_id='71-010-N1r',type='targeted proof check',outcome='d plus density gives disjointness and common frontier, hence c and the complementary-open formulation.'),dict(statement_id='71-010-N2 / corollary',type='targeted proof check',outcome='closure(X minus U_K)=(X minus U_K) union B proves local closedness iff B closed in X; closure B minus B subset C gives final criterion.')]
